Z||000000||Svyn||08-07-2001||10:21 PM||||Hello, I have a 86 Pontiac Fiero SE v6, I am a 3rd owner of the car and the previous owner was not sure what was wrong. Air will only come out of the Defrost Ducts, even the switch is turned off air comes out still. I am not able to change it to come out of the vent or floor ducts. Any ideas? Any additional information that you may need to help diagnose? I am at a loss...<BR>Thanks<BR><P>------------------<BR>-Dale Clark<BR>86' Fiero SE<BR>99' Dodge Durango SLT+<BR>92' Ford ThunderBird SuperCoupe||||reg||1
Z||000001||PBJ||08-07-2001||10:29 PM||||need to know if you have a/c with the push buttons or no a/c with the horizontal sliders.<P>If you have a/c it is an electrical mtr that does the work.<P>If you have no a/c a manual cable does the work-may have come off at either end.<P>Let us know??||||reg||1
Z||000002||Svyn||08-07-2001||11:17 PM||||Sorry, I do have the A/C with push buttons. Thanks much, any idea of price / part # for the motor ? Where is it, and tell me it doesn't require me to become gumby like replacing the sparkplug wires and other misc work on these =). <P>------------------<BR>-Dale Clark<BR>86' Fiero SE<BR>99' Dodge Durango SLT+<BR>92' Ford ThunderBird SuperCoupe<p>[This message has been edited by Svyn (edited 08-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||08-07-2001||11:21 PM||||For a start check all the fuses.<P>At the least you need a haynes book, which has the wiring diagrams, and the notes in my cave.<P>If the fuses are good either the control board has died or the mode motor behind the radio did.<P>||||reg||1
